Compile out Kimchi's self-update: Nix owns the binary, and the store copy is
read-only. The shared update gate is hardwired off, so background updates never
schedule ticks and the workflow finds no update for `kimchi update`, including
canary and explicit-version requests. `/update` stops before its menu (so no
toggle and no "enable auto-update" tip), the tip rotation drops the auto-update
tip, and the startup hook returns before bridge refresh, the one-time
auto-update notice or an "Update available" hint. Each gate is a one-line
condition, so the patch touches no import block or help text; `/update` keeps
upstream's notice wording.

